E["npc:crane-operator-bigglefuzz"] = {t="npc",n="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz",z="wailing",s="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz is a goblin dockhand working the heavy machinery at the port of Ratchet. After an overloaded crane mishap scattered cargo across the docks, he finds himself desperate to recover a valuable stolen bottle before his superiors notice.",h="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz is a goblin dockhand working the heavy machinery at the port of Ratchet.",sec={{t="Mishap on the Docks",b="Like many goblin dockworkers, Crane Operator Bigglefuzz prioritized efficiency and haste over basic safety margins. While attempting to hoist an excessively heavy haul from a merchant vessel, his crane buckled, sending crates crashing down across the Ratchet wharves. In the ensuing chaos, opportunistic scoundrels swept in, leaving Bigglefuzz to scramble to clean up the mess and salvage the most precious goods before Baron Revilgaz or the local port masters dock his pay.",sp=0},{t="The Stolen Port",b="The worst casualty of the accident was not the broken wood, but a crate containing rare ninety-nine-year-old port. Before Bigglefuzz could secure the spill, an elusive vagrant named Mad Magglish snatched a bottle and fled into hiding, threatening to leave Bigglefuzz answering for an irreplaceable loss.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Crane Operator Bigglefuzz?",a="He is a goblin crane operator stationed along the docks of Ratchet, responsible for loading and unloading sea cargo for the Steamwheedle Cartel.",al={"who is bigglefuzz","crane operator","bigglefuzz ratchet"}},{q="What caused the accident at the docks?",a="Bigglefuzz tried to hoist far too much weight at once with his crane, causing the machinery to fail and spilling cargo all over the wharf.",al={"why did the crane drop cargo","ratchet dock accident","crane mishap"}},{q="Who stole from Bigglefuzz?",a="A shifty troublemaker named Mad Magglish took advantage of the spilled freight to snatch a valuable bottle of ninety-nine-year-old port and slip away.",al={"who took the port","mad magglish cargo","who robbed bigglefuzz"}},{q="Why is Bigglefuzz so worried about the stolen bottle?",a="The ninety-nine-year-old port is extraordinarily rare and expensive. Losing it due to negligence means severe financial penalties or worse from the Steamwheedle Cartel bosses.",al={"why does bigglefuzz care about the wine","trouble at the docks reason"}}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers may appreciate that overloading Steamwheedle rigging and cranes remains the primary cause of industrial accidents along Kalimdor's coastlines.",["class:Rogue"]="Rogues can appreciate how quickly opportunistic thieves like Mad Magglish can exploit a moment of dockside confusion to lift priceless contraband right from under a goblin's nose."},kw={"bigglefuzz","cargo","crane operator","docks","mad magglish","port","ratchet","steamwheedle"},rel={"quest:959","subzone:ratchet","topic:goblin","zone:wailing"},src={"Crane Operator Bigglefuzz"}}
E["npc:ebru"] = {t="npc",n="Ebru",z="wailing",s="Ebru is a night elf druid sheltering in the crags above the Wailing Caverns. As one of Archdruid Naralex's few remaining uncorrupted disciples, she watches helplessly as her master's dream of restoring the Barrens curdles into a nightmare. From her perch, she enlists travelers brave enough to enter the subterranean depths to cull the mutated horrors spawned by the Nightmare.",h="Ebru is a night elf druid sheltering in the crags above the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="A Watch Above the Descent",b="While most of Archdruid Naralex's followers succumbed to the emerald corruption creeping through the caverns, Ebru managed to escape the nightmare's grasp. Camped inside the cavernous skull formation overlooking the entrance to the Wailing Caverns, she keeps vigil over the descent. She knows that Naralex's noble plan—to tap subterranean springs and transform the arid Barrens into lush woodland—has gone horribly awry, and she desperately directs willing adventurers to eliminate the burgeoning deviate beasts threatening to overrun the surrounding plains.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Corruption",b="The nightmare twisted not only the ecosystem of the caves, but also Ebru's fellow disciples, turning them into the fanatical Druids of the Fang. Stripped of her companionship and facing the ruin of her circle, Ebru focuses on containment. Items bearing her name, lost amidst the chaotic descent into madness, still circulate deep within the subterranean ecosystem, carried by mutated monstrosities that roam the dark.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Ebru?",a="Ebru is a night elf druid and an uncorrupted disciple of Archdruid Naralex. She resides in a cave high above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns, watching over the site and coordinating efforts to stem the corruption spilling out into the Barrens.",al={"who is ebru","ebru lore","about ebru"}},{q="Why is Ebru located above the Wailing Caverns?",a="She fled upward when Naralex's ritual collapsed into the Emerald Nightmare, turning her fellow disciples into hostile zealots. Her perch in the crag above the cave entrance allows her to monitor the caverns while staying safe from the feral horrors inside.",al={"where is ebru","why is ebru up here","ebru cave location"}},{q="What happened to Naralex and his other disciples?",a="Naralex entered a deep trance to tap the underground springs, but his mind became trapped within the Emerald Nightmare. The resulting corruption twisted the cave's flora and fauna and drove most of his disciples mad, transforming them into the Druids of the Fang.",al={"what happened to the disciples","naralex fate","druids of the fang origin"}},{q="What does Ebru ask travelers to do?",a="Ebru urges adventurers to delve into the depths of the Wailing Caverns to cull the deviate beasts and strike back against the mutated monstrosities born from her master's tormented dreams.",al={"ebru quests","deviate eradication","cleansing the caverns"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids of the Cenarion Circle, encountering Ebru is a stark reminder of the terrible dangers inherent in walking the Emerald Dream and the catastrophic cost of losing control.",["race:NightElf"]="Ebru represents the small, isolated enclave of night elves operating deep within the arid heart of Kalimdor, far from the ancient boughs of Ashenvale and Teldrassil."},kw={"barrens","cenarion circle","deviate","druid","ebru","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:naralex","quest:1487","zone:barrens","topic:night-elf"},src={"Ebru"}}
E["npc:lady-anacondra"] = {t="npc",n="Lady Anacondra",z="wailing",s="Lady Anacondra is one of the Fanglords leading the Druids of the Fang within the Wailing Caverns. Once a night elf acolyte named Scarletleaf, she was the first to volunteer for Naralex's ambitious effort to heal the Barrens. When her master's Emerald Dream communion turned into a nightmare, her mind broke, twisting her devotion into a venomous drive to see Kalimdor overrun by serpents.",h="Lady Anacondra is one of the Fanglords leading the Druids of the Fang within the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="From Scarletleaf to Serpent",b="Before adopting her serpentine title, Lady Anacondra was known as Scarletleaf. When the elder druid Naralex conceived of tapping into the subterranean springs of the Barrens through the Emerald Dream, she stepped forward as his very first volunteer. Her eager loyalty, however, proved her undoing. As Naralex's mind was seized by dark visions, the nightmare seeped out from the dreaming realm and contaminated his disciples, shattering Scarletleaf's sanity and reshaping her reverie into a cold, reptilian obsession.",sp=0},{t="A Fanglord in the Deep",b="Now styling herself Lady Anacondra, she stands guard among the first subterranean chambers of the Wailing Caverns. Like her fellow Fanglords, she abandoned the traditional tenets of the Cenarion Circle in favor of the vicious aspects of the viper. Channeling lightning, nature magic, and slumbering trances, she enforces Naralex's twisted slumber and works to spread the nightmare's corruption into the arid land above.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Lady Anacondra originally?",a="She was originally a young night elf acolyte named Scarletleaf. She was the very first disciple to volunteer to accompany the druid Naralex on his mission into the Barrens.",al={"anacondra real name","who is scarletleaf","scarletleaf backstory"}},{q="Why did she turn against the Cenarion Circle?",a="When Naralex attempted to connect to the Emerald Dream beneath the Barrens, his thoughts were overrun by a nightmare. That same nightmare infected the minds of his acolytes, corrupting Scarletleaf and driving her to cast aside her old life to serve the twisted dream.",al={"why is anacondra evil","how did she become a druid of the fang","why did scarletleaf fall"}},{q="What is her role in the Wailing Caverns?",a="She serves as one of the four Fanglords leading the Druids of the Fang. She guards the upper reaches of the caverns, ensuring that Naralex remains trapped in his corrupted sleep while dreaming of a reptilian future for the world.",al={"what does anacondra do","lady anacondra purpose","why kill anacondra"}},{q="Where can she be found inside the caverns?",a="Lady Anacondra wanders the first large network of caverns near the entrance of the Wailing Caverns. She patrols among the cavern's raptors and serpents, often shifting between a few resting spots.",al={"anacondra location","where is lady anacondra","anacondra spawn"}},{q="What item is taken from her for the Cenarion Circle?",a="She carries the Gem of Anacondra. Slaying her and claiming the gem is required by the Cenarion druids outside the caverns to break the Fanglords' hold over the oasis network.",al={"gem of anacondra","leaders of the fang anacondra","anacondra quest item"}},{q="What powers does she wield in battle?",a="She draws upon nature magic, striking her foes from afar with searing bolts of lightning and casting magical slumber to incapacitate invaders while her reptilian allies attack.",al={"anacondra abilities","anacondra spells","anacondra attacks"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Anacondra represents a cautionary tragedy for Cenarion druids: an earnest acolyte whose zeal to heal the land made her vulnerable to the nightmare that twisted her communion into madness.",["race:NightElf"]="Seeing a sister of Kaldorei lineage discard her heritage and form in pursuit of a twisted serpentine dream is a sobering reminder of the perils lurking within the Emerald Dream.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde cannot allow Anacondra and the Fanglords to threaten the delicate lifelines of the Barrens, making her removal critical to securing Crossroads and the nearby oases."},kw={"anacondra","barrens","druids of the fang","fanglord","gem of anacondra","lady anacondra","naralex","scarletleaf","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:naralex","topic:druids-of-the-fang","quest:914","zone:wailing","zone:barrens","topic:druid"},src={"Lady Anacondra"}}
E["npc:lord-cobrahn"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Cobrahn",z="wailing",s="Lord Cobrahn, formerly the night elf druid Jarlaxla, is one of the corrupted Druids of the Fang lurking deep within the Wailing Caverns. Once renowned within the Cenarion Circle for his mastery of shapeshifting, he succumbed to the nightmare infecting the cavern springs. Renaming himself after his new lethal guise, Cobrahn now commands broods of deviate serpents and defends the twisted labyrinth.",h="Lord Cobrahn, formerly the night elf druid Jarlaxla, is one of the corrupted Druids of the Fang lurking deep...",sec={{t="A Master of Forms Corrupted",b="Before adopting the moniker Lord Cobrahn, Jarlaxla was a respected member of the Cenarion Circle, celebrated among his fellow druids for his extraordinary skill in channeling animal forms. When Naralex ventured into the Wailing Caverns beneath the Barrens hoping to tap their underground springs and restore lush life to the arid wastes, Jarlaxla accompanied him. However, when Naralex's Emerald Dream communion decayed into a twisting nightmare, Jarlaxla's mind shattered alongside his brothers.",sp=0},{t="The Serpent's Embrace",b="Rather than channeling the traditional totemic beasts of Cenarion tradition, the nightmare warped Jarlaxla's shapeshifting prowess into something predatory and reptilian. Adopting the name Lord Cobrahn, he developed a deadly serpentine form that he unleashes in battle. Flanked by venomous deviate pythons and bearing a vicious clawed right hand, he oversees his section of the grottos, violently purging anyone seeking to break the nightmare's hold on the caverns.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Lord Cobrahn before he turned evil?",a="Lord Cobrahn was originally named Jarlaxla. He was a prominent night elf druid within the Cenarion Circle, widely respected for his rare talent and deep affinity for animal shapeshifting forms.",al={"cobrahn real name","who is cobrahn","jarlaxla"}},{q="Why is he called Lord Cobrahn?",a="Upon falling victim to the nightmare in the Wailing Caverns, Jarlaxla perfected a lethal serpentine shapeshifting form. He discarded his former name and took the title Lord Cobrahn to reflect his dangerous new power and mastery over serpents.",al={"why cobrahn","lord cobrahn name meaning"}},{q="Where can Lord Cobrahn be found?",a="Lord Cobrahn resides deep within the Wailing Caverns, a twisting underground network located in the central Barrens, surrounded by deviate pythons and other nightmare-corrupted beasts.",al={"cobrahn location","where is lord cobrahn","cobrahn room"}},{q="Why do adventurers need to defeat him?",a="He is one of the primary Fanglords leading the Druids of the Fang. He carries the Gem of Cobrahn, which is sought by Naralex's allies outside the cavern to break the nightmare's grasp on the underground springs.",al={"why kill cobrahn","leaders of the fang cobrahn"}},{q="What unique physical traits does he possess?",a="Unlike ordinary night elves, Cobrahn is noticeably larger in stature, wields a sharp claw on his right hand, and can transform completely into an oversized, venomous snake during combat.",al={"what does cobrahn look like","cobrahn appearance"}},{q="What is his connection to the other Druids of the Fang?",a="Cobrahn is one of the four key Fanglords alongside Lady Anacondra and their kin. They are former Cenarion Circle druids who entered the caverns with Naralex and jointly fell to the twisting corruption of the nightmare.",al={"druids of the fang leaders","cobrahn and anacondra"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Cobrahn serves as a grim warning of how druidic shapeshifting can be perverted when connected to the nightmare rather than natural balance.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Cobrahn's fall is a bitter tragedy, seeing a skilled brother of the Cenarion Circle abandon his heritage to lead monsters in the subterranean depths.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers seek Cobrahn to end the foul corruption leaking into the Barrens and protect the fragile ecosystem of Kalimdor's plains."},kw={"cobrahn","deviate python","druids of the fang","fanglord","gem of cobrahn","jarlaxla","lord cobrahn","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","quest:914","npc:lady-anacondra","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},src={"Lord Cobrahn"}}
E["npc:lord-pythas"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Pythas",z="wailing",s="Lord Pythas, once a night elf warrior named Aryn, is one of the four corrupted leaders of the Druids of the Fang in the Wailing Caverns. Originally a childhood friend and sworn protector of the archdruid Naralex, he fell victim to the nightmare tainting the oasis underground. Now he wields both martial might and twisted serpent magic against any who try to reach his slumbering master.",h="Lord Pythas, once a night elf warrior named Aryn, is one of the four corrupted leaders of the Druids of the...",sec={{t="A Guardian Falls",b="Before adopting the moniker Pythas, this night elf was known as Aryn. A seasoned warrior and trusted childhood companion to Naralex, he served as the archdruid's personal guard when the expedition ventured into the dry wastes of the Barrens. Eager to better serve Naralex's ambitious dream of restoring lush life to the arid realm, Aryn took up the study of druidism, proving to be an exceptionally fast learner. However, physical discipline and martial valor offered no shelter against the insidious corruption waiting deep within the subterranean fissures.",sp=0},{t="The Lethal Sentinel",b="When Naralex's connection to the Emerald Dream was hijacked by dark nightmares, Aryn's mind succumbed alongside those of his fellow acolytes. Shedding his former name and loyalty, he became Lord Pythas, leader among the Druids of the Fang. Where his fellow serpent lords favor cunning spellcasting or beast forms, Pythas seamlessly blends lethal combat prowess with nature magic. He now prowls the winding tunnels of the caverns, determined to defend the nightmare's twisted grip on the cavern spring.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Pythas?",a="Lord Pythas was originally a night elf warrior named Aryn. He was a childhood friend and personal bodyguard to Archdruid Naralex who studied druidism to assist his master's work in the Barrens.",al={"who is pythas","lord pythas lore","who was aryn"}},{q="Why did he turn against Naralex?",a="Pythas did not betray Naralex willingly. When Naralex attempted to tap into the Emerald Dream to heal the Barrens, a nightmare seized the archdruid's thoughts. The corrupting dream seeped into the minds of his acolytes, stripping away Aryn's sanity and remaking him into a serpent lord.",al={"why is pythas evil","how did pythas go mad","why did he become druid of the fang"}},{q="What makes Pythas different from the other Fang leaders?",a="Unlike the other leaders who rely purely on nature magic and beast forms, Pythas was a seasoned warrior before training as a druid. He combines martial combat skill with druidic magic, making him one of the most physically formidable defenders in the caverns.",al={"pythas fighting style","pythas vs other leaders"}},{q="Why do adventurers need to defeat him?",a="Pythas carries one of the four enchanted gems needed to complete the quest Leaders of the Fang. Naralex's surviving loyalists, the Disciple of Naralex, require the defeat of all four Fang leaders to disrupt the corruption and safely wake the sleeping archdruid.",al={"leaders of the fang quest","gem of pythas"}},{q="Where can Lord Pythas be found?",a="Lord Pythas lurks within the deep interior chambers of the Wailing Caverns, surrounded by corrupted beasts and fellow Fang cultists.",al={"pythas location","where is pythas"}},{q="What happens to his gem?",a="Upon his defeat, the Gem of Pythas is recovered from his remains. Adventurers bring it, along with the gems of the other three serpent lords, to Naralex's loyalists in the cave above the entrance to prove the leadership of the Fang has been broken.",al={"gem of pythas use","what is gem of pythas"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Pythas represents the tragic fate of a promising acolyte who embraced nature magic out of devotion, only to have the Emerald Dream's corruption twist his teachings into a viperous heresy.",["class:Warrior"]="Before he was corrupted into a serpent cultist, Pythas was a disciplined night elf warrior and personal protector—a grim reminder that martial prowess alone cannot stave off mental madness.",["race:NightElf"]="Watching a respected protector like Aryn fall to dark madness is a bitter sorrow for any night elf seeking to restore balance to the scarred soils of Kalimdor."},kw={"aryn","druids of the fang","gem of pythas","leaders of the fang","lord pythas","naralex","pythas","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:naralex","topic:druids-of-the-fang","quest:914","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},src={"Lord Pythas"}}
E["npc:lord-serpentis"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Serpentis",z="wailing",s="Lord Serpentis is a corrupted night elf druid who stands as the supreme leader of the rogue Druids of the Fang within the Wailing Caverns. Once the most promising disciple of the master druid Naralex, his lofty ambition twisted into madness when the Emerald Nightmare took hold of the subterranean springs. Now, he commands the serpent-worshipping sect and aggressively protects the slumbering teacher he failed to emulate.",h="Lord Serpentis is a corrupted night elf druid who stands as the supreme leader of the rogue Druids of the...",sec={{t="From Star Pupil to Serpent Lord",b="Before darkness overtook the cavern springs, Serpentis was revered as Naralex's finest and most capable apprentice. He possessed exceptional power and prestige among the Cenarion circle, driven primarily by an ambition to become an honored teacher—a shan'do—in his own right. However, when Naralex attempted to tap the subterranean water beneath the Barrens and fell prey to a corrupting nightmare, Serpentis's pride and ambition left his mind vulnerable to the emerging madness.",sp=0},{t="The Fang's Sovereign",b="Succumbing completely to the corruption radiating from Naralex's twisted dreams, Serpentis rallied his fellow apprentices to his side. Forsaking traditional Cenarion balance and the totem animals of old, they established the Druids of the Fang. Serpentis crowned himself lord of this new order, reshaping his brethren into serpent-worshipping zealots dedicated to spreading the nightmare rather than cleansing the Barrens.",sp=0},{t="The Final Obstacle",b="Perched deep inside the winding caverns, Lord Serpentis serves as the ideological and martial keystone of the rogue sect. As long as he lives, the Druids of the Fang remain united in their defense of the sleeping Naralex. Those seeking to wake the trapped master or reclaim the waters of the Oasis must strike down Serpentis and claim the gem he carries, breaking the serpent's hold over the labyrinth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Serpentis?",a="Lord Serpentis is the leader of the Druids of the Fang, located deep within the Wailing Caverns. Originally a high-ranking night elf druid and the foremost student of Naralex, he was corrupted by the Emerald Nightmare and took leadership of the fallen apprentices.",al={"who is serpentis","lord serpentis lore","serpentis background"}},{q="Why did Serpentis turn evil?",a="Serpentis desperately sought to achieve the status of a shan'do—an honored master. When Naralex fell into a corrupting trance beneath the Barrens, the Emerald Nightmare exploited Serpentis's ambition and pride, turning his mind toward madness and serpent worship.",al={"why did serpentis turn","serpentis corruption","why is serpentis bad"}},{q="What is his relationship to Naralex?",a="Serpentis was once Naralex's most gifted student. Rather than aiding in his master's recovery, Serpentis's twisted devotion led him to form the Druids of the Fang to protect Naralex's slumber and nurture the nightmare corrupting him.",al={"serpentis and naralex","is serpentis related to naralex","naralex apprentice"}},{q="Why do players need to kill him?",a="Serpentis is the supreme commander of the Druids of the Fang. Eliminating him is essential to break the sect's grip on the Wailing Caverns, secure his gem for the quest Leaders of the Fang, and clear a path toward awakening Naralex.",al={"why kill serpentis","leaders of the fang serpentis","gem of serpentis"}},{q="What does shan'do mean?",a="In Darnassian, shan'do translates to 'honored teacher.' It is a reverent title bestowed upon legendary druid instructors, such as Malfurion Stormrage or Naralex, and was the rank Serpentis obsessively wished to obtain.",al={"shando meaning","what is a shando","shan'do definition"}},{q="Who are the Druids of the Fang?",a="They are a renegade faction of night elf druids who followed Naralex into the Wailing Caverns. Corrupted by the Emerald Nightmare, they abandoned traditional druidic forms to adopt the aspects, venoms, and behaviors of serpents under Serpentis's command.",al={"druids of the fang lore","what are druids of the fang","fang druids"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Serpentis represents the tragic danger of unchecked ambition within the Cenarion Circle, showcasing what happens when a promising practitioner allows the Emerald Nightmare to twist the sacred bonds between student and shan'do.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Serpentis and his followers are a painful disgrace—kaldorei scholars of great renown who threw away their sacred duty to nature to become monstrous serpent lords.",["race:Tauren"]="Tauren see the corruption of Serpentis as a foul desecration of the Earth Mother's balance, threatening the fragile ecosystem of the Barrens with unnatural madness."},kw={"druids of the fang","gem of serpentis","leaders of the fang","lord serpentis","naralex","serpentis","shan'do","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:naralex","zone:wailing","quest:914","topic:druids-of-the-fang","topic:shan-do","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},src={"Lord Serpentis"}}
E["npc:mutanus-the-devourer"] = {t="npc",n="Mutanus the Devourer",z="wailing",s="Mutanus the Devourer is a monstrous, pale murloc manifested directly from the Emerald Nightmare. Lurking in the darkest recesses of the sleeping druid Naralex's mind, it emerges to devour anyone attempting to break the Nightmare's hold over the Wailing Caverns. Slaying this twisted aberration is the final step in freeing Naralex from his tormented slumber.",h="Mutanus the Devourer is a monstrous, pale murloc manifested directly from the Emerald Nightmare.",sec={{t="A Dreamer's Worst Fear",b="When the night elf druid Naralex tapped into the underground springs beneath the Barrens, he aimed to restore life to the arid wastes by connecting them to the Emerald Dream. Instead, an ancient corruption known as the Emerald Nightmare invaded his thoughts. Trapped in an agonizing vision, Naralex's subconscious fears took physical form. The corruption seized upon a bizarre, primal revulsion in the druid's psyche—his deep-seated terror of murlocs—and amplified it into an immense, albino predator.",sp=0},{t="The Waking Nightmare",b="Mutanus was sent forth into the waking world by the dark force infesting Naralex's mind, tasked with ensuring the druid never awakens. When a Disciple of Naralex performs the ritual to revive their master, Mutanus breaches the boundary between dream and reality. Along with his unnatural form, he brings alien relics from the dreamscape, such as the mysterious Deep Fathom Ring. Until Mutanus falls, Naralex remains a prisoner of his own corrupted imagination.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Mutanus the Devourer?",a="Mutanus the Devourer is an enormous, pale murloc-like aberration born from the Emerald Nightmare. He is not a normal denizen of Azeroth, but a living nightmare summoned into reality from the corrupted mind of the sleeping druid Naralex.",al={"who is mutanus","what kind of creature is mutanus","is mutanus a murloc"}},{q="Why does Mutanus look like a giant murloc?",a="The Nightmare twisted Naralex's subconscious thoughts and drew out his worst personal enemy: murlocs. The corruption weaponized that deep-seated fear, manifesting it as a colossal albino monstrosity.",al={"why murloc","why is mutanus a murloc","naralex murloc fear"}},{q="Why does Mutanus appear at the end of the ritual?",a="The dark presence corrupting the Emerald Dream ordered Mutanus to prevent anyone from breaking Naralex's slumber. When Naralex's disciples begin the awakening ritual, Mutanus crosses over into the physical cavern to devour the rescuers.",al={"when does mutanus spawn","why summon mutanus","naralex ritual boss"}},{q="Where does Mutanus come from?",a="Mutanus originates from the Emerald Nightmare, the corrupted realm that has ensnared Naralex. Crossing over from the dreamscape into Azeroth, he even brought along strange relics like the Deep Fathom Ring.",al={"mutanus origin","is mutanus from the nightmare","emerald nightmare mutanus"}},{q="Does killing Mutanus save Naralex?",a="Yes. Once Mutanus is slain, the nightmare's immediate hold over Naralex's mind is shattered, allowing his disciples to successfully awaken the druid and break the cavern's dark trance.",al={"is naralex saved","what happens after mutanus dies","waking naralex"},sp=1},{q="Why is Mutanus immune to shadow magic?",a="Mutanus is an aberration woven from dark nightmare energies, making him naturally resilient against necrotic and shadow spells that would harm mundane beasts.",al={"mutanus shadow immunity","shadow spells mutanus","is mutanus shadow immune"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Mutanus represents the terrifying hazards of delving too deeply into the Emerald Dream without safeguards, as a fellow druid's mind was completely overtaken by corruption.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, Mutanus is a tragedy brought to life, embodying how Naralex's noble ambitions to heal the Barrens warped into a monstrous nightmare.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde cannot allow Mutanus and the Nightmare to corrupt the heart of the Barrens, threatening the vital oasis waters needed to sustain Durotar and Mulgore."},kw={"albino murloc","barrens","deep fathom ring","devourer","emerald nightmare","murloc","mutanus","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:naralex","zone:wailing","topic:emerald-dream","topic:murloc","topic:druid"},src={"Mutanus the Devourer"}}
E["npc:nalpak"] = {t="npc",n="Nalpak",z="wailing",s="Nalpak is a tauren druid disciple who watches over the troubled Wailing Caverns in the Barrens. Stationed in the high cliff-cave overlooking the cavern entrance, he enlists passing adventurers to help contain the nightmare twisting the subterranean ecosystem.",h="Nalpak is a tauren druid disciple who watches over the troubled Wailing Caverns in the Barrens.",sec={{t="Watcher Above the Caverns",b="Perched inside a hidden cavern directly above the mouth of the Wailing Caverns, Nalpak remains loyal to the vision of Archdruid Naralex. While his master lies trapped in a corrupted slumber deep below, Nalpak works to keep the spreading corruption at bay. Rather than descending blindly into the darkness, he charges resourceful adventurers with gathering materials from the mutated fauna, such as the hides of deviate beasts, to study and counteract the unnatural transformation overtaking the oasis.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Nalpak located?",a="Nalpak is located in a cave high up on the rock face directly above the natural rock formation that leads into the Wailing Caverns in the central Barrens.",al={"nalpak location","where is nalpak","find nalpak"}},{q="Who is Nalpak?",a="He is a tauren druid and one of the Disciples of Naralex, tasked with monitoring the emergence of twisted creatures from the Wailing Caverns while his master attempts to restore the Barrens through the Emerald Dream.",al={"who is nalpak","nalpak lore"}},{q="Why does Nalpak want deviate hides?",a="Nalpak collects deviate hides from the corrupted raptors, crocolisks, and vipers inside the caves to study the unnatural mutations wrought by the Emerald Nightmare and assist his fellow druids in clothing and protecting their expedition.",al={"why deviate hides","deviate hides quest"}},{q="What is Nalpak's relationship to Naralex?",a="Nalpak is a faithful student and follower of Archdruid Naralex, serving as one of the disciples sent to support the ambitious attempt to reawaken the springs of the Barrens.",al={"is nalpak naralex disciple","nalpak and naralex"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For fellow druids, Nalpak is a grim reminder of how perilous touching the Emerald Dream can be when darkness takes root in what was meant to be a restorative ritual.",["race:Tauren"]="Nalpak represents the tauren dedication to healing the parched lands of Kalimdor, refusing to abandon the mission even when disaster strikes the dreamers."},kw={"barrens druid","deviate hides","disciples of naralex","nalpak","naralex","tauren","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:naralex","zone:wailing","quest:1486","zone:barrens","topic:tauren"},src={"Nalpak"}}
E["npc:naralex"] = {t="npc",n="Naralex",z="wailing",s="Naralex is a night elf druid who sought to restore the parched Barrens to a lush forest using the powers of the Emerald Dream. Instead, his slumber was overtaken by a dark nightmare, twisting the Wailing Caverns beneath the earth and turning his followers into venomous fiends.",h="Naralex is a night elf druid who sought to restore the parched Barrens to a lush forest using the powers of...",sec={{t="A Vision of Green",b="Long before the Great Sundering, the sun-scorched plains of the Barrens were once a vibrant forest. Viewing this loss as a tragedy, Naralex journeyed south from Darnassus with a cohort of devoted disciples to reverse the drought. Deep beneath the savannah, he discovered an intricate subterranean network of underground springs and rushing geysers, naming them the Wailing Caverns after the howling wind and steam that moaned through the rock. He believed that by entering a deep trance and channeling the pristine energies of the Emerald Dream into these subterranean waters, the life-giving flow would reach the surface and cause the entire wasteland to bloom.",sp=0},{t="The Waking Nightmare",b="Naralex seated himself in deep meditation deep within the subterranean caverns, but his noble design collapsed the moment his consciousness touched the realm of the Dream. Rather than finding peaceful fonts of wild nature, his mind was ensnared by a malignant, encroaching corruption—an Emerald Nightmare. The festering corruption seized the sleeping druid's body, transforming him into an open conduit through which dark energies bled into the living world. The pristine springs turned foul, sprouting mutated fungal blooms and warping the native beasts of the caverns into ravenous deviate horrors.",sp=0},{t="Fallen Disciples",b="The nightmare did not stop with the wildlife. Naralex's own disciples, driven completely mad by the psychic backlash bleeding out of their master's trance, broke away from the traditions of the Cenarion Circle. Casting aside their reverence for balance, they took on serpent forms and renamed themselves the Druids of the Fang. Believing their twisted growth must spread across Kalimdor, they now guard Naralex's slumbering body to ensure he never wakes, leaving only a lone loyal disciple named Muyoh searching for allies brave enough to break the trance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Naralex?",a="Naralex is a night elf druid of the Cenarion Circle. He led an expedition into the Wailing Caverns with the goal of tapping into the Emerald Dream to turn the arid Barrens back into the lush forest it had been before the Sundering.",al={"naralex lore","who is the sleeping elf","wailing caverns sleeper"}},{q="Why is Naralex asleep inside the Wailing Caverns?",a="He entered a meditative trance to channel energies directly from the Emerald Dream into the underground aquifers beneath the Barrens. However, an overwhelming nightmare seized his mind, trapping him in a fevered slumber that he cannot wake from on his own.",al={"why is naralex sleeping","what is naralex doing","naralex trance"}},{q="What created the Druids of the Fang?",a="They were originally Naralex's faithful disciples. When the Emerald Nightmare corrupted Naralex's dream connection, the leaking malice drove his followers insane. They abandoned the Cenarion Circle, embraced serpent totems, and now protect his slumber to keep the corruption spreading.",al={"druids of the fang origin","who are druids of the fang","naralex disciples"}},{q="What caused the Wailing Caverns to mutate?",a="Naralex's sleeping body became an open conduit for the Emerald Nightmare. The foul dream energies seeped directly into the subterranean river system, warping the caverns' plants, crocodiles, raptors, and serpents into aggressive deviate mutants.",al={"why is wailing caverns corrupted","deviate beasts origin","wailing caverns fungus"}},{q="Can Naralex be awakened?",a="Yes, with outside help. His remaining loyal disciple, Muyoh, works with adventurers willing to enter the depths, slay the twisted Druids of the Fang, and perform a ritual to break the grip of the nightmare on Naralex's mind.",al={"how to save naralex","waking naralex","naralex quest"},sp=1},{q="Why did Naralex want to change the Barrens?",a="Naralex learned that the Barrens was once a flourishing forest before the Great Sundering shattered Kalimdor. He saw its current arid condition as an ecological wound and wished to restore its ancient verdant canopy.",al={"why regrow the barrens","naralex barrens goal","why the barrens"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Naralex serves as a grim cautionary tale to druids: meddling blindly with primal natural states or tapping too deeply into the Dream without caution can unleash catastrophic perversions of the wild.",["race:NightElf"]="While Naralex sought to heal Kalimdor, his unchecked ambition deep in Horde territory brought disgrace to the Cenarion Circle and spawned the treacherous Druids of the Fang.",["race:Tauren"]="The twisted waters beneath the Barrens pose an immediate threat to the oasis pools and wildlife that sustain the tribes of Mulgore and the savannah.",["faction:Horde"]="A night elf's failed mystical experiment has polluted the heart of the Barrens, forcing Horde forces from the Crossroads to deal with the rampaging beasts boiling up from the cavern."},kw={"cenarion circle","deviate","druids of the fang","emerald dream","emerald nightmare","muyoh","naralex","the barrens","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","topic:druids-of-the-fang","topic:emerald-dream","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid","zone:barrens","topic:night-elf","quest:1489"},src={"Naralex"}}
E["npc:verdan-the-everliving"] = {t="npc",n="Verdan the Everliving",z="wailing",s="Verdan the Everliving is a colossal bog beast lurking deep within the verdant tunnels of the Wailing Caverns. Once a peaceful protector of the underground springs and flora, he was twisted by the waking nightmare radiating from the sleeping druid Naralex. Now bound to the corrupted Druids of the Fang, Verdan violently attacks any who venture into his damp hollows.",h="Verdan the Everliving is a colossal bog beast lurking deep within the verdant tunnels of the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Lush Depths",b="Long before Naralex arrived to tap into the natural springs of the Barrens, Verdan was formed from the overgrown foliage, silt, and moisture filling the caves. Thought to be the original guardian spirit of the subterranean oasis, Verdan was an ancient, gentle elemental keeping watch over the underground flora.",sp=0},{t="Twisted by the Nightmare",b="When Naralex attempted to cultivate the dry Barrens into a lush paradise, his ritual fractured into a vivid nightmare within the Emerald Dream. The resulting corruption bled through the subterranean waters, tainting everything living inside the cavern. Verdan could not resist the pervasive blight; his gentle temperament vanished, leaving behind an enormous, hostile brute sworn to protect the mad Druids of the Fang.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What kind of creature is Verdan?",a="Verdan is a massive bog beast, an elemental being animated out of plant matter, peat, and subterranean mire. He formed naturally from the rich flora of the caves long ago.",al={"verdan monster type","what is verdan","verdan race"}},{q="Why is Verdan hostile to adventurers?",a="Verdan was once a peaceful guardian of the caverns, but the nightmare emanating from the slumbering Archdruid Naralex corrupted his mind. Now maddened, he perceives all outside intruders as trespassers to be crushed.",al={"why does verdan attack","verdan hostile","is verdan evil"}},{q="What is Verdan's connection to the Druids of the Fang?",a="Both Verdan and the Druids of the Fang fell victim to the same corrupting nightmare. Sharing this twisted vision, Verdan acts as an ally and enforcer for the insane druids, guarding the deeper reaches of the caverns.",al={"verdan druids of the fang","verdan fang connection"}},{q="Where in the Wailing Caverns is Verdan located?",a="Verdan dwells in a cavernous, mossy chamber deep in the winding paths of the Wailing Caverns, past several of the corrupted Fang leaders.",al={"where is verdan","verdan location","how to find verdan"}},{q="Can Verdan be cured or cleansed?",a="There is no known way to cleanse Verdan. The nightmare took deep root in his elemental form, leaving adventurers no choice but to destroy the hulking beast to ensure safe passage through the cavern.",al={"can verdan be saved","save verdan","purify verdan"}},{q="Why was Verdan called 'the Everliving'?",a="As an elemental manifestation of the enduring flora and underground waters of the cave, he was an ancient being that naturally renewed itself over untold ages, living far beyond the lifespan of mortal creatures.",al={"why everliving","everliving meaning","verdan name origin"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Verdan's fall is a tragic reminder of what happens when natural elemental wardens are poisoned by a corrupted Emerald Dream.",["class:Shaman"]="As an elemental spirit of earth and water grown warped and violent, putting down Verdan is an act of restoring balance to the fractured elements of the Barrens.",["faction:Horde"]="Because the Wailing Caverns sit at the heart of the Barrens, defeating dangerous beasts like Verdan is essential to protecting nearby crossroads and settlements."},kw={"bog beast","druids of the fang","elemental","everliving","naralex","nightmare","verdan","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:naralex","quest:1012","topic:druid"},src={"Verdan the Everliving"}}
E["quest:1486"] = {t="quest",n="Deviate Hides",z="wailing",s="Deviate Hides is a task given by Nalpak, a disciple of Naralex stationed above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns. While Naralex lies trapped in a twisted nightmare, Nalpak seeks to salvage something useful from the mutated beasts spawned beneath the Barrens. By gathering skins from these deviate predators, he hopes to put their strange, otherworldly properties to practical use.",h="Deviate Hides is a task given by Nalpak, a disciple of Naralex stationed above the entrance to the Wailing...",sec={{t="Corruption Made Manifest",b="When the night elf druid Naralex attempted to tap the subterranean springs beneath the Barrens to restore lush life to the arid plains, his mind slipped into a terrifying nightmare. That dark reverie bled into reality, mutating the native wildlife of the Wailing Caverns into vicious deviate beasts. Raptors, crocolisks, vipers, and shambling horrors emerged warped and aggressive, altered by the emerald corruption leaking from their dreaming master.",sp=0},{t="A Pragmatic Druid",b="Perched in the rock formation above the cavern mouth, Nalpak watches the disaster unfold with a mix of dread and practical curiosity. Though he recognizes the deviate creatures as inherently malignant and unnatural, he believes their corrupted forms might yield unique materials. In particular, their toughened, warped pelts possess resilience that could benefit skilled leatherworkers, turning the fruits of a tragic nightmare into durable equipment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Nalpak?",a="Nalpak and his fellow disciples have established a small camp high up in the rock formation resembling a skull above the Wailing Caverns entrance. Rather than walking straight into the main tunnel, climb the mountain slopes behind the cave mouth and carefully drop down into the upper cavern eye-socket ledge overlooking the oasis.",al={"nalpak location","where is nalpak","how to find nalpak","quest giver deviate hides"}},{q="What are deviate creatures?",a="Deviate creatures are local beasts transformed by the Emerald Nightmare that escaped from Naralex's slumbering mind. Raptors, snakes, crocolisks, and wind serpents native to the Barrens have been twisted into darker, vicious forms with strange magical properties and mottled, unnatural hides.",al={"what are deviates","deviate beasts","why are animals mutated in wailing caverns"}},{q="Why does Nalpak want these hides?",a="Nalpak recognizes that while the beasts are born of evil corruption, their hides exhibit unusual, otherworldly strength. He believes that by studying and working the pelts, leatherworkers can repurpose the nightmare's taint into resilient gear.",al={"why deviate hides","what does nalpak want hides for","purpose of deviate hides"}},{q="Can any deviate creature drop the hides?",a="The mutated beasts prowling throughout the tunnels and interior of the Wailing Caverns carry these skins. Hunters and leatherworkers often find skinning the beasts yields extra pelts beyond what can simply be scavenged from their remains.",al={"which mobs drop deviate hides","who drops deviate hide","deviate hide farm"}},{q="Is Nalpak aligned with the Horde or the Alliance?",a="Nalpak is a disciple of Naralex and belongs to the Cenarion Circle. He remains neutral and will accept aid from any capable adventurer, whether Alliance or Horde, who is brave enough to enter the corrupted caves.",al={"is nalpak horde","is deviate hides alliance","can alliance do deviate hides"}},{q="What happened to Naralex?",a="Naralex sought to awaken the underground springs of the Barrens by connecting his consciousness to the Emerald Dream. Instead, his slumber was seized by the Nightmare, transforming the cavern system into a breeding ground for horrors and leaving him comatose deep within the caves.",al={"who is naralex","naralex nightmare","what happened to the druid in wailing caverns"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Nalpak's camp represents the Cenarion Circle's grim vigil over an initiative gone terribly wrong, making the task of containing the cavern's mutations personal for fellow druids.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The abnormal growth feeding the deviate beasts is directly tied to the corrupted flora and underground springs winding through the cavern network."},kw={"barrens","cenarion circle","deviate","deviate hides","emerald nightmare","leatherworking","nalpak","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:nalpak","zone:wailing","npc:naralex","zone:barrens"},m={start="Nalpak",level="17",faction="Neutral",id=1486},src={"Deviate Hides (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1487"] = {t="quest",n="Deviate Eradication",z="wailing",s="Deviate Eradication is a task assigned by the night elf druid Ebru above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns. While other disciples focus on waking their slumbering leader, Ebru asks adventurers to purge the caverns of mutated deviate beasts spawned by his twisted vision. Ridding the subterranean oasis of these horrors is an essential step in stemming the corruption threatening the Barrens.",h="Deviate Eradication is a task assigned by the night elf druid Ebru above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="A Dream Gone Terribly Wrong",b="The night elf druid Naralex brought his followers to the subterranean springs of the Barrens with an ambitious vision: tap into the Emerald Dream to regrow the parched plains into a lush, thriving woodland. Instead, Naralex became ensnared within the Dream, his slumber twisting into an agonizing nightmare. Rather than healing the land, the power surging through the caverns warped the native wildlife and plant life into monstrous, aggressive mutants known as deviate beasts.",sp=0},{t="Ebru's Stand",b="Perched in the cliff-face cavern overlooking the cave entrance, Ebru and a handful of surviving Disciples of Naralex watch in despair as their numbers dwindle. While some among them dedicate their energy toward awakening their fallen master, Ebru recognizes an immediate crisis. Left unchecked, the rapidly multiplying deviate vipers, shamblers, ravagers, and dreadfangs will spill outward into the Barrens. Ebru therefore recruits passing adventurers to descend into the deep tunnels and cull the aberrant monstrosities at their source.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find Ebru to start this quest?",a="Ebru is stationed with a few fellow Disciples of Naralex in a secluded cave perched high above the main mouth of the Wailing Caverns, resting inside what resembles the right eye socket of the skull-shaped rock formation. Reaching her typically requires climbing around the mountain ridge and carefully dropping down onto the upper ledge.",al={"ebru location","where is ebru","how to get to ebru","wailing caverns eye cave"}},{q="What caused the beasts to become deviate?",a="The creatures were mutated by dark energies seeping from the Emerald Dream. When the druid Naralex linked his consciousness to the subterranean springs to rejuvenate the Barrens, his mind was hijacked by a nightmare, warping the restorative energies into a corrupting force that mutates local wildlife into deviate monsters.",al={"why are they deviate","deviate beasts origin","what corrupted the animals in wc"}},{q="Who are the Disciples of Naralex?",a="The Disciples of Naralex are a circle of druidic followers who accompanied Naralex to the Wailing Caverns to help revitalize the Barrens. Following his entrapment within the Nightmare, many turned feral or fell into madness, leaving only a tiny remnant of sane disciples trying to undo the disaster.",al={"disciples of naralex","naralex followers","who are the druids in wailing caverns"}},{q="Can Alliance and Horde both take this quest?",a="Yes. Ebru and her companions are neutral druids concerned with the preservation of nature and the containment of the Nightmare. They accept assistance from capable champions of either the Horde or the Alliance.",al={"deviate eradication alliance or horde","is deviate eradication neutral"}},{q="What creatures do you have to slay for Ebru?",a="Ebru directs you to hunt down four specific breeds of corrupted fauna deep within the caverns: Deviate Ravagers, Deviate Vipers, Deviate Shamblers, and Deviate Dreadfangs, slaying seven of each.",al={"deviate eradication mobs","deviate eradication targets","which deviate to kill"}},{q="Does completing this quest wake Naralex?",a="No. Ebru's assignment focuses strictly on pest control and damage mitigation by thinning out the dangerous beasts. Awakening Naralex requires a direct ritual performed deep inside his sanctum at the heart of the cavern.",al={"does this wake naralex","how to wake naralex"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The twisted ecosystem within the caverns serves as a somber warning of what happens when communion with the Emerald Dream turns disastrous.",["faction:Horde"]="Because the Wailing Caverns sit in the very heart of Kalimdor's central plains, culling these aggressive predators is vital to protecting nearby settlements like the Crossroads.",["race:NightElf"]="Witnessing Naralex's noble aspiration collapse into nightmare-born horror is a heavy burden for kaldorei travelers, who feel a duty to assist their stranded kin."},kw={"barrens","deviate dreadfang","deviate eradication","deviate ravager","deviate shambler","deviate viper","ebru","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:ebru","npc:naralex","zone:wailing","zone:barrens","topic:emerald-dream"},m={start="Ebru",level="21",faction="Neutral",id=1487},src={"Deviate Eradication"}}
E["quest:1489"] = {t="quest",n="Hamuul Runetotem",z="wailing",s="This quest directs Horde adventurers from the lush but troubled oases of the Barrens to the lofty heights of Thunder Bluff. Tonga Runetotem suspects a deep spiritual corruption within the Wailing Caverns and sends you to seek the guidance of Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem.",h="This quest directs Horde adventurers from the lush but troubled oases of the Barrens to the lofty heights of...",sec={{t="A Disturbing Dream",b="While studying the wildlife of the Barrens, Tonga Runetotem identified a strange affliction gripping the creatures near the lush oases. The altered beasts carried shells tainted by an unnatural force, leading Tonga to realize that the land itself is trapped in a delirious, troubled dream. Convinced that the waters flowing from the subterranean Wailing Caverns are the origin of this rot, Tonga knows that venturing inside requires far greater wisdom than a lone naturalist possesses.",sp=0},{t="Counsel on Elder Rise",b="To understand the threat within the caverns, Tonga directs you to Thunder Bluff to confer with his kin, Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem. Hamuul is the highest-ranking tauren druid and a revered spiritual leader of the Cenarion Circle in Mulgore. Stationed atop the tranquil Elder Rise, Hamuul monitors disturbances across Kalimdor and confirms that the nightmare seeping through the Barrens is a dire threat demanding the full might of Horde champions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Tonga send me to Hamuul?",a="Tonga discovered that the Barrens' oases are tainted by a bizarre affliction emerging from the Wailing Caverns. Because the phenomenon feels like a nightmare gripping the earth, he sends you to Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem on Elder Rise for high-level druidic guidance before anyone attempts to enter the caverns.",al={"why hamuul","why talk to hamuul","hamuul quest purpose"}},{q="Where is Hamuul Runetotem located?",a="Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem is located in Thunder Bluff, the capital city of the tauren in Mulgore. He stands atop the Elder Rise, overlooking the surrounding plains alongside other druids and shamans.",al={"hamuul location","where is hamuul","find hamuul runetotem"}},{q="What is the source of the taint Tonga noticed?",a="The taint stems from the underground springs of the Wailing Caverns. The strange waters are corrupting local wildlife and flora, causing the land to behave as if it is trapped in an inescapable nightmare.",al={"what is the taint","oasis corruption","wailing caverns taint"}},{q="What happens after speaking with Hamuul?",a="Hamuul welcomes you to Thunder Bluff and prepares you for the trials ahead. He warns that dealing with the nightmare beneath the Barrens is a dire endeavor and directs you to Nara Wildmane to prepare for the descent into the Wailing Caverns.",al={"next quest after hamuul","what next","hamuul follow up"}},{q="Who is Hamuul Runetotem?",a="Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem is the foremost leader of the tauren druids and a close childhood friend and advisor to High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof. Having learned the ways of the wild following the Third War, he guides tauren druids into communion with nature and the Cenarion Circle.",al={"who is hamuul","hamuul lore","archdruid hamuul"}},{q="Is this quest required to enter the Wailing Caverns?",a="No attunement is required to physically step into the Wailing Caverns, but this quest is the Horde narrative bridge linking the mystery of the Barrens' lush oases to the expedition inside the dungeon.",al={"wailing caverns attunement","is this quest mandatory"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For tauren druids, reporting to Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem is a pilgrimage to the mentor who established modern tauren druidism under Malfurion Stormrage's teachings.",["race:Tauren"]="The mission bridges concerns in the ancestral hunting grounds of the Barrens with the guidance of the tribal elders dwelling atop the sacred bluffs of Mulgore.",["faction:Horde"]="As the Barrens serves as the crossroad of the young Horde, investigating the spreading taint protects the supply lines connecting Durotar, Mulgore, and the northern outposts."},kw={"elder rise","hamuul runetotem","oases","taint","the barrens","thunder bluff","tonga runetotem","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:tonga-runetotem","subzone:elder-rise","zone:thunderbluff","zone:wailing","zone:barrens","topic:druid"},m={start="Tonga Runetotem",["end"]="Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem",level="16",faction="Horde",id=1489},src={"Hamuul Runetotem (quest)"}}
E["quest:1490"] = {t="quest",n="Nara Wildmane",z="wailing",s="Nara Wildmane is a young tauren druid in Thunder Bluff seeking to unravel the tragedy unfolding deep within the Wailing Caverns. After Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem peered into the Emerald Dream and withdrew from the corruption festering there, he dispatched adventurers to confer with Nara, whose fierce spirit endured long enough to witness the nightmare taking hold of their kin. She serves as the pivotal Horde contact directing champions to put an end to the Druids of the Fang.",h="Nara Wildmane is a young tauren druid in Thunder Bluff seeking to unravel the tragedy unfolding deep within...",sec={{t="A Vision of Corruption",b="When strange, unnatural phenomena began spreading across the Barrens, Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem journeyed into the Emerald Dream to discern the cause. There he witnessed a cult of druids who had originally sought to restore life to the arid savannah, only to lose their minds to a vile taint. Being aged and unable to linger long against the nightmare's assault, Hamuul fled back to the waking world. However, his younger disciple, Nara Wildmane, refused to yield so easily. Her fiery resolve kept her anchored in the dreamscape far longer, allowing her to observe the transformed cult firsthand.",sp=0},{t="Confronting the Nightmare",b="While Hamuul provides the overarching guidance for the Cenarion Circle in Thunder Bluff, Nara Wildmane possesses the tactical insight needed to purge the rot. Having stared directly upon the twisted, serpent-scaled countenances of the fallen druids, she knows their crimes and the devastation they intend to unleash upon Kalimdor. Her resolve marks the beginning of the Horde's offensive into the Wailing Caverns to eliminate the leaders who abandoned their sacred oaths.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Nara Wildmane?",a="Nara Wildmane is a young and spirited tauren druid residing on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. She studies under Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem and is unafraid to confront the corrupting nightmares threatening the balance of nature.",al={"who is nara","nara wildmane lore","nara wildmane thunder bluff"}},{q="Why does Hamuul Runetotem send travelers to speak with her?",a="Hamuul admits that his advanced age and failing strength prevented him from lingering within the corrupted dream where the Druids of the Fang reside. Because Nara is young and fiercely determined, she stayed in the dreaming realm longer and gathered vital intelligence on the cult's plans.",al={"why speak with nara","hamuul to nara","why hamuul send me here"}},{q="What did Nara see in the Emerald Dream?",a="Nara bore witness to the fallen druids dwelling in the Wailing Caverns. She saw their faces twisted into serpentine, scaled visages and perceived the dark plots and crimes they intend to enact upon the Barrens.",al={"what did nara see","nara dream vision","scaled druids dream"}},{q="Where can Nara Wildmane be found?",a="She can be found in a druidic tent situated atop the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, just across from Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem.",al={"where is nara","nara wildmane location","find nara wildmane"}},{q="What happens after reporting to Nara Wildmane?",a="Once you speak with her, Nara instructs you to enter the Wailing Caverns and slay the rogue Druids of the Fang, setting up the major dungeon quest 'Leaders of the Fang'.",al={"next quest after nara","what does nara want me to do","leaders of the fang follow up"}},{q="Why are the druids in the Wailing Caverns corrupted?",a="Led by Naralex, the druids entered the caverns hoping to tap into the Emerald Dream and bring lush life to the Barrens. Instead, Naralex's slumber twisted into a horrific nightmare, ensnaring his followers and twisting them into the serpentine Druids of the Fang.",al={"wailing caverns cult","druids of the fang why evil","why barrens druids evil"}}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren who have recently embraced the path of druidism under Hamuul, Nara represents the young, unyielding generation willing to confront unnatural blight head-on.",["class:Druid"]="Druids will appreciate Nara's courage in navigating the treacherous, corrupted reaches of the Emerald Dream where even veteran masters like Hamuul hesitated to linger.",["faction:Horde"]="Nara's vigilance protects the heart of Horde territory, ensuring that the dark energies twisting the Barrens do not spread unchecked into Mulgore."},kw={"barrens","druids of the fang","elder rise","emerald dream","hamuul runetotem","nara wildmane","thunder bluff","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","quest:914","topic:druid","zone:barrens"},m={start="Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem",["end"]="Nara Wildmane",level="16",faction="Horde",id=1490},src={"Nara Wildmane (quest)"}}
E["quest:1491"] = {t="quest",n="Smart Drinks",z="wailing",s="Smart Drinks is an entrepreneurial scheme cooked up by the goblin merchant Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet. Having failed to brew an intellect-enhancing tonic out of Sunscale raptor horns, Mebok now tasks adventurers with delving into the Wailing Caverns to harvest ectoplasmic residue for his latest beverage formula.",h="Smart Drinks is an entrepreneurial scheme cooked up by the goblin merchant Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",sec={{t="A Recipe for Disaster",b="Operating out of the bustling port town of Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix embodies the classic goblin philosophy of turning any bizarre regional phenomenon into cold, hard coin. Convinced that an intellect-boosting draught will make him an overnight tycoon, he originally believed powdered raptor horns held the secret. When that batch proved thoroughly underwhelming, he simply set his sights on an even more dubious ingredient: the corrupting essence seeping out of the nearby Wailing Caverns.",sp=0},{t="The Wailing Essence",b="The Barrens have experienced unsettling ecological mutations, with lush oases abruptly sprouting and local wildlife warping into aggressive horrors. Mizzyrix theorizes that a strange substance he calls 'Wailing Essence' is the catalyst behind these sudden shifts. Concluding that whatever alters biology so intensely must make a potent secret ingredient, he dispatches mercenaries to destroy the oozing ectoplasms dwelling deep within the cavern labyrinth and siphon their glowing fluid straight into beverage bottles.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mebok Mizzyrix?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix is an enterprising goblin stationed in the port town of Ratchet. Unbothered by health codes, he is obsessed with creating a commercial 'smart drink' to sell across Kalimdor and strike it rich.",al={"mebok mizzyrix","who gives smart drinks","smart drinks quest giver"}},{q="Why didn't the raptor horns work?",a="Mebok originally believed that grinding up horns from Sunscale raptors would produce a potent intellect-boosting concoction. The resulting beverage failed to deliver the promised genius, forcing him to pivot to a far more dangerous active ingredient.",al={"why raptor horns failed","raptor horn drink"}},{q="What is Wailing Essence?",a="Wailing Essence is an ectoplasmic substance found dripping from the unnatural slimes deep inside the Wailing Caverns. Mebok believes this volatile matter is the driving catalyst behind the bizarre botanical and animal mutations spreading through the Barrens.",al={"what is wailing essence","essence from wailing caverns"}},{q="Where do you find the ectoplasms carrying the essence?",a="The essence is gathered from ectoplasmic creatures such as evolving, devouring, and nightmare ectoplasms that lurk inside the underground tunnels of the Wailing Caverns, located west of Ratchet.",al={"where are ectoplasms","smart drinks mobs","who drops wailing essence"}},{q="Is the smart drink safe to consume?",a="Considering the essence is harvested from nightmarish slimes linked to corrupting mutations across the Barrens, bottling it as a commercial tonic is wildly reckless. True to goblin business ethics, Mebok is far more concerned with marketability than customer safety.",al={"is smart drink poisonous","does the drink work"}},{q="What comes after completing Smart Drinks?",a="Smart Drinks concludes Mebok's immediate beverage venture. Satisfied with your delivery of Wailing Essence, he rewards you and promises to share future profits once his dubious tonic makes him a fortune.",al={"smart drinks follow up","what next after smart drinks"}}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Any culinarian will immediately spot the health code catastrophe unfolding in Ratchet: steeping raw, nightmare-tainted ectoplasm directly into a drinkable tonic violates every standard of food safety.",["class:Druid"]="While druids enter the Wailing Caverns to cleanse the nightmare twisting the emerald dreamscape, Mebok sees the tragic ecological taint merely as cheap liquid syrup for his retail venture.",["faction:Horde"]="For travelers navigating through the crossroads of the Barrens, Ratchet's merchants offer plenty of quick coin, provided you do not ask too many questions about what they plan to do with the monster parts you deliver."},kw={"barrens","ectoplasm","mebok mizzyrix","raptor horns","ratchet","smart drinks","wailing caverns","wailing essence"},rel={"npc:mebok-mizzyrix","quest:865","zone:wailing","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},m={start="Mebok Mizzyrix",level="18",id=1491},src={"Smart Drinks"}}
E["quest:6981"] = {t="quest",n="The Glowing Shard",z="wailing",s="The Glowing Shard is a mysterious emerald-hued gem plucked from the dark depths of the Wailing Caverns. Swirling with smoky essence beneath its polished surface, this disturbing relic drives adventurers to seek answers in Ratchet and beyond.",h="The Glowing Shard is a mysterious emerald-hued gem plucked from the dark depths of the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="A Disturbing Discovery",b="Drawn from deep within the Wailing Caverns, the glowing shard immediately unnerves those who hold it. Brilliant green and seemingly solid, it holds churning, mist-like shadows beneath its crystalline face. The crystal exerts a subtle pull, demanding attention while exuding a deeply unsettling aura that hints at the corrupted nature of the slumbering druids and their nightmare-infested sanctuary.",sp=0},{t="Seeking Answers in Ratchet",b="Uncertain of the stone's origin or nature, adventurers bring the artifact to the goblin port of Ratchet. There, local engineer Sputtervalve inspects the oddity, only to recognize that its origins lie beyond the scope of goblin machinery and standard geology. Instead, he directs seekers up into the rocky ridges above the caverns, where the tauren mystic Falla Sagewind watches over the troubled spirits of the Barrens.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Glowing Shard?",a="It is a corrupted, luminescent green crystal found deep within the Wailing Caverns. Inside its glassy shell, faint smoke swirls, unsettling anyone who studies it closely.",al={"glowing shard item","what is this green gem","shard from wailing caverns"}},{q="Who can examine the shard in Ratchet?",a="Sputtervalve, an engineer stationed near the flight master in Ratchet, examines the shard. Though he is an engineer rather than a druid, he recognizes its strange energy and points you toward someone with spiritual expertise.",al={"who in ratchet looks at shard","ratchet npc for shard","sputtervalve shard"}},{q="Where is Falla Sagewind located?",a="Falla Sagewind makes her camp on the mountain peaks directly above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns in the central Barrens.",al={"falla sagewind location","where is falla","mountain above wailing caverns"}},{q="Does Sputtervalve have a quest marker over his head?",a="No. Sputtervalve does not display an active quest icon. You must speak with him directly and select the dialogue prompt regarding the strange glowing shard to advance.",al={"sputtervalve no question mark","cant turn in to sputtervalve","sputtervalve bugged"}},{q="Why does the shard look like it contains smoke?",a="The smoky swirl within the crystal reflects the pervasive corruption warping the Wailing Caverns, tied directly to the Emerald Nightmare invading the thoughts of the slumbering Druids of the Fang.",al={"why does shard smoke","green smoke in gem","corruption in shard"}},{q="Who can complete the quest chain after Falla Sagewind?",a="Both Horde and Alliance adventurers can pursue this storyline. Falla Sagewind's findings lead directly into the quest 'In Nightmares', sending heroes to seek guidance from their respective leaders and elders.",al={"is this quest horde only","alliance glowing shard","who gets in nightmares"},sp=1}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids, the shard's emerald sheen and smoky core are grim evidence of the Emerald Nightmare seeping into the waking world through their fallen brethren in the Wailing Caverns.",["race:Tauren"]="The balance of the Barrens is dear to the Shu'halo, and bringing this unnatural relic to Falla Sagewind aids in understanding the corruption poisoning their ancestral lands.",["faction:Horde"]="Unraveling the mystery of the shard helps protect the vital crossroads and trade routes of the Barrens from unnatural threats festering in the underground springs.",["faction:Alliance"]="Even far from home in Kalimdor, Alliance explorers recognize the global peril posed by whatever dark power is corrupting nature beneath the Barrens."},kw={"barrens","druids of the fang","emerald nightmare","falla sagewind","glowing shard","ratchet","sputtervalve","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:sputtervalve","npc:falla-sagewind","quest:3369","subzone:ratchet","topic:goblin","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},m={start="Glowing Shard",["end"]="Falla Sagewind",level="26",id=6981},src={"The Glowing Shard"}}
E["quest:914"] = {t="quest",n="Leaders of the Fang",z="wailing",s="Leaders of the Fang is a pivotal Horde quest tasked by Nara Wildmane from the heights of Thunder Bluff. It directs adventurers into the Wailing Caverns to strike down the four leaders of the corrupted Druids of the Fang and retrieve their twisted dream gems. Halting these rogue druids is essential to preventing their serpentine nightmare from permanently overtaking the Barrens.",h="Leaders of the Fang is a pivotal Horde quest tasked by Nara Wildmane from the heights of Thunder Bluff.",sec={{t="A Vision Corrupted",b="The night elf archdruid Naralex ventured into the subterranean springs of the Wailing Caverns with a selfless ambition: to use the Emerald Dream to restore lush vitality to the arid Barrens. Tragically, when his slumber took root, his dream turned into a waking nightmare. The acolytes who accompanied him lost their devotion to nature's harmony, succumbing to malignant serpent spirits and adopting the mantle of the Druids of the Fang.",sp=0},{t="The Four Dream Gems",b="To reshape the Barrens into their own viperous Eden, the leaders of the splintered sect channel the warped dream energies through specialized foci known as dream gems. Lord Cobrahn, Lady Anacondra, Lord Pythas, and Lord Serpentis each bear one of these gems. As long as these artifacts remain in their grasp, their corrupting influence will seep outward into the soil and waters of Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="A Burden Lifted in Thunder Bluff",b="Nara Wildmane, watching over the natural balance from Thunder Bluff, feels the spiritual torment rippling from the caverns directly into her mind. By hunting down the four serpent lords and stripping them of their gems, Horde champions break the sect's command structure, freeing the tauren druid from lingering nightmares and saving the surrounding plains from an unnatural blight.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who are the leaders of the Druids of the Fang?",a="The sect is guided by four fallen druids: Lady Anacondra, Lord Cobrahn, Lord Pythas, and Lord Serpentis. Each has surrendered their original nature teachings to embody serpent forms and channel nightmare magic within the Wailing Caverns.",al={"leaders of the fang names","wailing caverns bosses","who leads druids of the fang"}},{q="What are the dream gems?",a="The dream gems are conduits carried by each of the four leaders within the Wailing Caverns. They focus the twisted, nightmare-tainted energy leaking from Naralex's slumber, fueling the sect's efforts to mutate the Barrens.",al={"what are the gems","gem of cobrahn","dream gems lore"}},{q="Why does Nara Wildmane want the gems?",a="Nara Wildmane is a tauren druid in Thunder Bluff who feels the psychic and spiritual ripples of the nightmare. The faces of the corrupted leaders haunt her dreams, and she needs their power broken to protect both her sanity and the future of the Barrens.",al={"who is nara wildmane","why kill the leaders","nara wildmane motive"}},{q="Were the Druids of the Fang always evil?",a="No. They were originally noble night elf druids who followed Naralex into the caverns hoping to heal the dry savanna. When Naralex fell into a nightmare, the energies warped their minds, transforming them into a fanatical snake cult.",al={"druids of the fang origin","why did the druids turn bad","naralex disciples"}},{q="Where is this quest turned in?",a="The quest begins and ends with Nara Wildmane on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. Once you collect all four gems from the depths of the Wailing Caverns, you must travel back to Mulgore to present them to her.",al={"leaders of the fang turn in","where is nara wildmane","hand in leaders of the fang"}},{q="Does killing the leaders cure Naralex?",a="Slaying the four leaders shatters the sect's upper hierarchy and stops the spread of their ritual, but it does not wake Naralex on its own. Other druidic rites deeper within the caverns are required to awaken the slumbering master.",al={"does this save naralex","killing leaders effect"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For tauren druids, this mission is deeply personal. Seeing fellow servants of nature twist the Emerald Dream into a poisonous blight is an intolerable affront to Cenarion principles.",["faction:Horde"]="The Barrens is the vital crossroads connecting Orgrimmar, Thunder Bluff, and the Darkspear isles. Allowing a fanatical sect of serpent worshipers to mutate the land threatens the stability of the entire Horde.",["race:Tauren"]="The Earth Mother's health is central to tauren faith, making the unnatural corruption bleeding from the springs of the Barrens a direct sacrilege against the land they roam."},kw={"anacondra","barrens","cobrahn","dream gems","leaders of the fang","nara wildmane","pythas","serpentis","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","topic:druids-of-the-fang","quest:1490","zone:barrens","zone:thunderbluff","topic:druid"},m={start="Nara Wildmane",level="22",faction="Horde",id=914},src={"Leaders of the Fang"}}
E["quest:959"] = {t="quest",n="Trouble at the Docks",z="wailing",s="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz caused a clumsy cargo accident on the Ratchet docks, allowing a petty troublemaker named Mad Magglish to snatch a priceless vintage bottle. The vintage—a 99-Year-Old Port sent directly from Baron Revilgaz to Gazlowe—must be recovered from the shadows of the Wailing Caverns before the dockmaster fires the negligent crane operator.",h="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz caused a clumsy cargo accident on the Ratchet docks, allowing a petty troublemaker...",sec={{t="A Clumsy Mishap",b="Ratchet thrives on constant sea trade with Booty Bay across the Great Sea, but its goblin efficiency occasionally cracks under sheer volume. When an unusually massive morning shipment arrived at the port, Crane Operator Bigglefuzz tried to cut corners to speed up the unloading process. Lifting far more than his crane could manage, he dropped the entire haul across the docks. In the ensuing chaos, a local nuisance named Mad Magglish took advantage of the spilled crates, snatched a single valuable bottle of liquor, and fled inland.",sp=0},{t="Diplomatic Vintage",b="The stolen cargo was far more than an ordinary ration of dockside spirits. The bottle was a 99-Year-Old Port sent as a personal diplomatic gift from Baron Revilgaz, the notorious Blackwater ruler of Booty Bay, to Gazlowe, the chief engineer and overseer of Ratchet. Losing such a lavish offering threatens to humiliate Bigglefuzz and enrage both trade moguls. Faced with losing his job or worse, Bigglefuzz tracked the thief to the ominous mouth of the Wailing Caverns, though fear kept him from following Magglish inside.",sp=0},{t="The Cavern Hideout",b="Rather than venturing deep into the corrupted dreamscape of the dungeon itself, Mad Magglish chose to hide within the sprawling, damp natural tunnels outside the inner gateway. Relying on clumsy stealth and dark alcoves, Magglish skulks through the subterranean caverns hoping pursuers will give up. Retrieving the port requires flushing out the thief from the outer reaches before the vintage is uncorked or destroyed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this bottle of port so important?",a="The 99-Year-Old Port is not ordinary grog; it is an extravagant personal gift sent by Baron Revilgaz of Booty Bay to Gazlowe, the boss of Ratchet. Losing it in a dock mishap threatens to deeply anger Ratchet's leadership and cost Crane Operator Bigglefuzz his livelihood.",al={"why does bigglefuzz care","what is the 99-year-old port","why is the wine important"}},{q="Who is Mad Magglish?",a="Mad Magglish is an opportunistic thief and troublemaker hanging around Ratchet. When Bigglefuzz dropped a massive cargo load on the docks, Magglish grabbed the rare bottle of port and fled straight into the nearby Wailing Caverns to hide.",al={"who is magglish","who stole the port","mad magglish lore"}},{q="Do I have to enter the Wailing Caverns dungeon to find the thief?",a="No. Mad Magglish hides in the winding, public cave passages outside the instance portal. He uses weak stealth and lurks in the upper side tunnels or near the flooded chambers leading toward the main entrance.",al={"is magglish inside the instance","where is mad magglish","find magglish"}},{q="How did the cargo spill happen?",a="A massive cargo shipment arrived from Booty Bay, and Crane Operator Bigglefuzz tried to unload more crates at once than his equipment could handle. The overloaded crane dropped the haul, scattering valuable freight across the Ratchet docks.",al={"why did the crates drop","what did bigglefuzz do","crane mishap ratchet"}},{q="What is the relationship between Ratchet and Booty Bay?",a="Both port towns are vital strongholds of the Steamwheedle Cartel, bound by commerce and privateer fleets. Regular trade shipments and formal courtesies pass between Baron Revilgaz in the south and Gazlowe in the Barrens to maintain their mutual trade empire.",al={"ratchet and booty bay connection","steamwheedle ports","revilgaz and gazlowe"}},{q="Why didn't Bigglefuzz retrieve the bottle himself?",a="Bigglefuzz pursued the thief right to the entrance of the Wailing Caverns, but the eerie reputation and monstrous inhabitants of the underground labyrinth terrified the goblin into stopping at the threshold.",al={"why didn't the goblin get it","why did bigglefuzz stop chasing"}}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Hunting Mad Magglish is an exercise in spotting sloppy concealment, as the thief relies on rudimentary stealth within the cavern crannies to escape notice.",["faction:Horde"]="Assisting Ratchet's dockhands helps maintain smooth operations for the primary neutral port connecting Kalimdor to the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though operating deep within the Horde-dominated Barrens, staying on the good side of Steamwheedle port operators ensures safe passage through neutral waters."},kw={"bigglefuzz","booty bay","gazlowe","magglish","port","ratchet","revilgaz","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:crane-operator-bigglefuzz","subzone:ratchet","zone:wailing","npc:baron-revilgaz","subzone:booty-bay","zone:barrens"},m={start="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz",level="18",id=959},src={"Trouble at the Docks"}}
E["quest:962"] = {t="quest",n="Serpentbloom",z="wailing",s="Serpentbloom is a gathering task issued by Apothecary Zamah, an envoy of the Royal Apothecary Society residing in Thunder Bluff. Zamah seeks specimens of a rare herb native to the subterranean depths of the Wailing Caverns to aid the research of the Forsaken.",h="Serpentbloom is a gathering task issued by Apothecary Zamah, an envoy of the Royal Apothecary Society...",sec={{t="Eyes of the Apothecary",b="Perched upon the Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff, Apothecary Zamah serves as an envoy of the Royal Apothecary Society from the Undercity. While the tauren hosts focus on spiritual balance and healing the wounded land, Zamah's attention is fixed on rare and virulent materials. Having isolated a sample of an unusual plant known as Serpentbloom, she seeks bulk quantities to advance the research directives of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken.",sp=0},{t="The Depths of the Caverns",b="Serpentbloom does not grow under the open sun of the Barrens, thriving instead in the damp, twisting grottos of the Wailing Caverns. Cultivated in the humid subterranean climate twisted by the corrupted druids of the Fang, the plant is difficult to reach and fiercely guarded by the cavern's serpentine denizens. Zamah readily admits that numerous scouts sent before failed to return, leaving further harvesting to hardened adventurers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Zamah?",a="Apothecary Zamah is a researcher representing the Royal Apothecary Society of the Undercity. Stationed in Thunder Bluff on the Spirit Rise, she acts as a liaison between the Forsaken alchemists and the wider continent of Kalimdor.",al={"zamah","apothecary zamah lore","who gives serpentbloom"}},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society want Serpentbloom?",a="Zamah believes the herb possesses significant latent chemical potential when refined in large quantities. The Society actively searches across Kalimdor for rare, potent flora that can aid the Forsaken's alchemical experiments.",al={"why serpentbloom","forsaken herb research","purpose of serpentbloom"}},{q="Where does Serpentbloom grow?",a="Serpentbloom grows exclusively inside the subterranean reaches of the Wailing Caverns, nestled within the damp rock corridors and subterranean passages carved beneath the northern Barrens.",al={"where is serpentbloom","serpentbloom location"}},{q="Why haven't previous scouts returned?",a="The Wailing Caverns are overrun by devolved beasts, raptors, and the corrupted Druids of the Fang. Less experienced foragers sent into the labyrinthian tunnels were quickly overwhelmed by the cavern's predatory fauna and venomous defenders.",al={"missing scouts","zamah's scouts","is wailing caverns dangerous"}},{q="Do the Tauren approve of Zamah's research?",a="The tauren of Thunder Bluff granted the Forsaken sanctuary out of sympathy and a desire to heal them, but the alchemical practices of the Royal Apothecary Society often skirt close to unnatural experimentation that makes traditional shamans and druids uneasy.",al={"tauren reaction","spirit rise apothecaries"}},{q="Does harvesting Serpentbloom require herbalism skills?",a="No. While it is a botanical specimen, any adventurer willing to brave the depths of the Wailing Caverns can pluck the plants directly from the cave floor without formal herbalism training.",al={"do i need herbalism","gather serpentbloom profession"}}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Contributing Serpentbloom directly supports the Royal Apothecary Society's alchemical initiatives in Lordaeron under the Dark Lady's mandate.",["race:Tauren"]="Hosting Forsaken apothecaries upon the Spirit Rise reflects the Horde's hospitality, even as their focus on lethal concoctions contrasts with traditional earth healing.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The twisted environment inside the Wailing Caverns fosters unique flora found nowhere else on the sunbaked surface of the Barrens.",["faction:Horde"]="This task cements the early operational alliance between the Undercity and the Kalimdor tribes, sharing resources and rare reagents across the ocean."},kw={"apothecary","barrens","royal apothecary society","serpentbloom","spirit rise","thunder bluff","undercity","wailing caverns","zamah"},rel={"quest:853","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:wailing","zone:thunderbluff","topic:forsaken","zone:undercity","zone:barrens"},m={start="Apothecary Zamah",level="18",faction="Horde",id=962},src={"Serpentbloom (quest)"}}
E["subzone:cavern-of-mists"] = {t="subzone",n="Cavern of Mists",z="wailing",s="The Cavern of Mists is the expansive outer antechamber leading into the depths of the Wailing Caverns. Fed by subterranean geysers that erupt through the rock, its central pool and hanging fog harbor strange, mutated wildlife roaming just outside the portal threshold.",h="The Cavern of Mists is the expansive outer antechamber leading into the depths of the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="The Threshold of the Nightmare",b="Before descending into the true heart of the Wailing Caverns, travelers must navigate the Cavern of Mists. Thick, warm vapor hangs permanently in the air, fed by natural geysers erupting from the cavern floor into a deep central pool. Though it serves as an entryway, it is far from peaceful. Swarms of raptors, serpents, oozes, and semi-aquatic threshadons wander the ledges and waters, alongside notorious beasts like the hydra Trigore the Lasher. It provides adventurers an ominous preview of the unnatural growth festering deeper below.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Cavern of Mists?",a="The Cavern of Mists comprises the outer cave system of the Wailing Caverns, located southwest of the Crossroads in the Barrens. It is the non-instanced chamber that players must traverse to reach the instance portal itself.",al={"cavern of mists location","where is cavern of mists","wailing caverns entrance cave"}},{q="Why is it called the Cavern of Mists?",a="Active geysers constantly burst from the stone floor, feeding the central pool and filling the subterranean air with heavy, humid fog.",al={"why misty","cavern of mists name origin"}},{q="What creatures live here?",a="The chamber is populated by raptors, oozes, wind serpents, snakes, toads, and threshadons inhabiting the pool, as well as occasional sightings of the rare hydra Trigore the Lasher.",al={"mobs in cavern of mists","cavern of mists monsters"}},{q="Who is Trigore the Lasher?",a="Trigore the Lasher is a dangerous rare hydra that can occasionally be found swimming alongside the threshadons in the chamber's central pool.",al={"trigore","hydra rare wailing caverns"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The twisted wildlife thriving in the heavy vapors gives Cenarion druids their first warning of how deeply Naralex's Emerald Dream communion has gone astray.",["faction:Horde"]="Resting right in the heart of the Barrens, clearing out the predatory beasts lurking in these mists is critical to securing the trade routes and outposts around the Crossroads."},kw={"barrens","cavern of mists","geysers","threshadons","trigore the lasher","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","quest:938"},src={"Cavern of Mists"}}
E["subzone:crag-of-the-everliving"] = {t="subzone",n="Crag of the Everliving",z="wailing",s="The Crag of the Everliving is a verdant cavern chamber nestled deep within the Wailing Caverns. Dominated by lush, corrupted flora and predatory plant creatures, it serves as the domain of the Fanglord Lord Pythas. Its towering upper reaches shelter the ancient entity after whom the crag is named.",h="The Crag of the Everliving is a verdant cavern chamber nestled deep within the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="A Corrupted Canopy",b="While much of the Wailing Caverns is carved of damp subterranean stone, the Crag of the Everliving bursts with unruly, twisted vegetation fueled by the Nightmare corrupting Naralex's slumber. Towering mossy platforms and winding paths are choked with Deviate Shamblers—living plant hulks prowling the undergrowth. Lord Pythas, one of Naralex's fallen disciples, watches over the crag's central reaches, having traded his noble druidic vows for the venomous rites of the Druids of the Fang.",sp=0},{t="The Ancient Guardian",b="The chamber draws its name from Verdan the Everliving, a colossal, primordial plant elemental who resides in the crag's upper heights. Corrupted by the Emerald Nightmare that grips the cavern, Verdan now acts as a fearsome line of defense rather than a peaceful natural guardian. Beyond his towering form lurks Lord Serpentis, the self-proclaimed chief of the Fanglords, who oversees the sect's descent into serpentine madness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this area get its name?",a="The chamber is named after Verdan the Everliving, an ancient and colossal plant beast residing in the highest terraces of the crag. Though once an embodiment of nature's timeless vitality, he has fallen under the sway of the Nightmare that afflicts the caverns.",al={"why crag of the everliving","everliving name origin","crag name"}},{q="Who controls this part of the caverns?",a="Lord Pythas, one of the primary Fanglords, directly presides over the crag. In the higher ledges above him lurk both Verdan the Everliving and Lord Serpentis, the leader of the Druids of the Fang.",al={"who is in charge here","crag boss","fanglord here"}},{q="What creatures are commonly found in the Crag of the Everliving?",a="The crag is overrun with Deviate Shamblers—shambling plant horrors birthed from the corrupted springs—alongside twisted serpents and the fanatical Druids of the Fang.",al={"monsters in crag","crag enemies","what lives here"}},{q="Why is plant life thriving so deep underground?",a="The underground springs were harnessed by the night elf druid Naralex to rejuvenate the Barrens. When his ritual was snared by the Emerald Nightmare, the wild growth ran rampant and twisted into hostile, aberrant flora.",al={"why are there plants underground","why so green","corrupted greenery"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Seeing the Crag of the Everliving is a tragic lesson for Cenarion druids, as pure natural vitality and elemental guardianship have been warped into lethal tools of the Nightmare.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The crag's unnaturally lush subterranean atmosphere nourishes rare underground roots and mushrooms that flourish in the humid, dream-soaked soil."},kw={"barrens","crag of the everliving","deviate shamblers","druids of the fang","lord pythas","lord serpentis","verdan","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:lord-pythas","npc:verdan-the-everliving","npc:lord-serpentis"},src={"Crag of the Everliving"}}
E["subzone:dreamer-s-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Dreamer's Rock",z="wailing",s="Dreamer's Rock is a secluded natural sanctuary tucked deep within the Wailing Caverns past the Screaming Gully. Here lies the sleeping night elf druid Naralex, whose noble effort to revive the Barrens has instead birthed a living nightmare. It serves as both a sacred barrow chamber and the epicenter of the corruption mutating the surrounding subterranean ecosystem.",h="Dreamer's Rock is a secluded natural sanctuary tucked deep within the Wailing Caverns past the Screaming...",sec={{t="The Slumber of Naralex",b="Located in the heart of the Wailing Caverns, Dreamer's Rock functions much like an improvised barrow den. Here, the night elf druid Naralex entered a deep trance to tap the underground springs and channel the Emerald Dream into the arid soil of the Barrens. Instead of bringing life, his connection was seized by dark forces. The nightmare twisting his thoughts now spills physically into this chamber, twisting the local wildlife, turning his followers into the venomous Druids of the Fang, and manifesting terrifying aberrations into the waking world.",sp=0},{t="The Awakening Ritual",b="Only by ending the corruption of the Fanglords can a surviving Disciple of Naralex venture to Dreamer's Rock to perform the ritual of waking. The process is fraught with peril: as the chant begins, Naralex's lingering nightmare manifests monstrosities to defend its hold over his sleeping mind. The ultimate culmination of this psychic torment is Mutanus the Devourer, a vile aberration that materializes directly from the depths of the dreamer's subconscious to consume all who seek to free him.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is sleeping at Dreamer's Rock?",a="Naralex, a powerful night elf druid, lies in slumber here. He came to the Wailing Caverns hoping to harness its subterranean water channels to restore lush life to the Barrens, but his communion with the Emerald Dream was hijacked by terrible nightmares.",al={"sleeping elf","who is asleep here","who is naralex","dreamer identity"}},{q="Why is this chamber called Dreamer's Rock?",a="The chamber is named for Naralex himself, 'the Dreamer.' Acting much like a traditional night elf barrow den, it provides the physical resting place for his body while his spirit traverses the Dream.",al={"why dreamers rock","dreamers rock name meaning","name origin"}},{q="What happens when you try to wake Naralex?",a="Once the Fanglords throughout the caverns are slain, a loyal Disciple of Naralex comes to the rock to begin an awakening chant. The nightmare violently resists being broken, sending waves of shadow-tainted beasts and finally the monstrous Mutanus the Devourer into the waking world.",al={"waking naralex","disciple ritual","naralex event"},sp=1},{q="Why did Naralex's followers turn hostile?",a="As Naralex's communion turned into a nightmare, the dark visions warped the minds of his acolytes. Abandoning their Cenarion vows, they embraced serpent aspects, becoming the Druids of the Fang and zealously defending their master's tormented, unending sleep.",al={"druids of the fang origin","why are the druids evil","corrupted druids"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Dreamer's Rock stands as a grim warning of the dangers lurking within the Emerald Dream, showing how easily noble intentions can be subverted by slumbering horrors.",["race:NightElf"]="Finding a sacred barrow-style resting chamber corrupted beneath the arid Barrens is a somber reminder of the tragic risks Naralex and his followers took far from Kalimdor's northern forests."},kw={"barrow den","dreamer's rock","dreamers rock","druids of the fang","emerald dream","mutanus","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:naralex","zone:wailing","npc:mutanus-the-devourer","subzone:screaming-gully","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},src={"Dreamer's Rock"}}
E["subzone:screaming-gully"] = {t="subzone",n="Screaming Gully",z="wailing",s="Screaming Gully is the first sprawling subterranean cavern encountered just beyond the entrance of the Wailing Caverns. Bathed in unnatural fungal glow and shallow waters, it serves as the outer redoubt for the corrupted Druids of the Fang and their mutated beasts.",h="Screaming Gully is the first sprawling subterranean cavern encountered just beyond the entrance of the...",sec={{t="Threshold of the Nightmare",b="Stepping through the threshold of the Wailing Caverns leads directly into Screaming Gully, an echoing chasm where the wind groans through subterranean fissures. Far from the arid Barrens above, the gully is choked with damp overgrowth, humid mist, and aggressive wildlife twisted by the Emerald Nightmare. The Fanglord Lady Anacondra oversees the chamber, surrounded by acolytes of the Druids of the Fang and vicious deviate raptors, while ancient snapping turtles like Kresh patrol the shallow waterways below.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Screaming Gully located?",a="The Screaming Gully is the first major chamber you enter directly after stepping through the portal inside the Wailing Caverns, located beneath the northern Barrens.",al={"screaming gully location","where is screaming gully","how to find screaming gully"}},{q="Why is it called the Screaming Gully?",a="The Wailing Caverns earn their name from the howling, moaning sounds caused by subterranean steam and winds venting through rock fissures, and this wide entrance chasm catches the brunt of those echoing cries.",al={"why screaming gully","screaming gully name origin"}},{q="Who rules over the Screaming Gully?",a="The chamber is overseen by Lady Anacondra, one of the primary Fanglords who fell under the corruption of the Emerald Nightmare alongside Naralex.",al={"screaming gully boss","who is in screaming gully","screaming gully leader"}},{q="What creatures roam this chamber?",a="The gully is populated by deviate raptors, corrupted Druids of the Fang, and wandering aquatic life, including the ancient turtle Kresh roaming the flooded floor.",al={"screaming gully mobs","enemies in screaming gully"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For Cenarion druids, Screaming Gully is a heartbreaking display of their fallen brethren who abandoned the path of the claw and sky to embrace serpentine corruption."},kw={"barrens","deviate raptor","fanglords","kresh","lady anacondra","screaming gully","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:lady-anacondra","topic:druids-of-the-fang","topic:druid"},src={"Screaming Gully"}}
E["zone:wailing"] = {t="dungeon",n="Wailing Caverns",z="wailing",s="Tucked beneath the Lushwater Oasis in the arid Barrens lies the Wailing Caverns, a labyrinthine system of subterranean springs and fissures named for the eerie whistling of trapped steam. What began as a noble druidic effort to revitalize Kalimdor's sun-bleached savanna has devolved into a warped, poisonous underworld. The caverns now teem with twisted wildlife and fallen disciples corrupted by a deep, unnatural nightmare.",h="Tucked beneath the Lushwater Oasis in the arid Barrens lies the Wailing Caverns, a labyrinthine system of...",sec={{t="A Noble Vision Turned Poisonous",b="The night elf druid Naralex originally discovered this vast water system and devised an ambitious design: by opening a conduit straight into the Emerald Dream, he would siphon pure primal life essence through the subterranean springs, transforming the parched Barrens back into a thriving, verdant paradise. Deep in the Cavern of Mists, Naralex slipped into communion with the Dream, anchored by his loyal acolytes. Tragically, rather than tapping into pure vitality, the druid's sleeping mind touched the Emerald Nightmare. The festering corruption instantly seized him, transforming his well-intentioned conduit into a valve pouring venom and madness into the underground waterways.",sp=0},{t="The Druids of the Fang",b="As the Nightmare's dark energy radiated from Naralex's helpless form, his students succumbed to the madness. Forsaking the tranquil wisdom of the Cenarion Circle, they formed the fanatical Druids of the Fang. Taking reptilian forms, the sect's leaders—Lady Anacondra, Lord Cobrahn, Lord Pythas, and Lord Serpentis—now embrace the venomous mutation of the caverns rather than fighting it. They actively shield their sleeping master from any outside interference, believing this twisted growth is the true evolution of nature.",sp=0},{t="The Nightmare Made Flesh",b="Breaking the grip of the Druids of the Fang does not automatically save Naralex. When his remaining uncorrupted disciples initiate the ritual to gently rouse him from his trance at Dreamer's Rock, the slumbering elf's thrashing subconscious violently purges its deepest terror. The creature that erupts forth—a monstrous, distorted murloc named Mutanus the Devourer—is the physical manifestation of Naralex's worst nightmares. Only by slaying this abomination can the channel to the Nightmare be snapped, freeing Naralex to wake, assume avian form, and take flight from the tainted caves.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is it called the Wailing Caverns?",a="The cavern earns its name from the mournful, howling cries heard throughout the tunnels. These sounds are produced naturally when subterranean steam vents and high-pressure gusts of wind force their way through tight fissures in the limestone rock.",al={"why wailing caverns","name origin","why do they wail"}},{q="What caused the beasts inside to become 'deviate'?",a="When Naralex fell under the sway of the Emerald Nightmare, the tainted dream energies bled directly into the underground springs. Drinking and living in these contaminated waters mutated the natural raptors, crocolisks, and serpents into unnatural 'deviate' variants.",al={"deviate corruption","why are raptors mutate","deviate beasts origin"}},{q="Who are the Druids of the Fang?",a="They were once the devoted night elf and tauren acolytes of Naralex. Corrupted alongside him by the Nightmare, their minds shattered and twisted their druidic arts into worship of serpents and venom, adopting titles like Cobrahn, Pythas, and Anacondra.",al={"fang druids","druids of the fang lore","who is serpentis"}},{q="Why is the final boss a giant murloc named Mutanus?",a="Mutanus the Devourer is not a standard denizen of the caverns, but an ectoplasmic entity birthed from the Emerald Nightmare itself. As the waking ritual takes hold, Naralex's slumbering mind purges the horrific manifestation of his subconscious fear into physical reality.",al={"why mutanus murloc","what is mutanus","final boss lore"},sp=1},{q="What happens after Mutanus is defeated?",a="Once Mutanus is struck down, the psychic stranglehold on Naralex shatters. The night elf druid awakens from his horrific trance, transforms into a stormcrow, and flies out of the caverns to safety alongside his surviving disciple, finally ending the active channel into the Nightmare.",al={"waking naralex","naralex ending","what happens to naralex"},sp=1},{q="Who is living in the cave above the cavern entrance?",a="Perched inside the cavern's skull-like rock eye socket are Cenarion Circle loyalists, including Nalpak and Ebru. They seek brave travelers to harvest deviate hides and cleanse the corruption before it completely engulfs the Barrens.",al={"cave above entrance","snake skull eye npcs","who is nalpak and ebru"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids of both Cenarion tradition and the tauren walk, the caverns are a tragic warning of the perils within the Emerald Dream and a solemn duty to purge their fallen brethren, the Druids of the Fang.",["race:Tauren"]="The twisted waters threaten the fragile oases that sustain life across the Barrens, making the cleansing of the springs vital to the tribes of Mulgore and the Crossroads.",["race:NightElf"]="Naralex was a revered figure among night elf druids, and the tragedy of his corruption by the Emerald Nightmare represents a painful catastrophe for his kin across the sea."},kw={"deviate","druids of the fang","emerald nightmare","lady anacondra","lord cobrahn","lord pythas","lord serpentis","lushwater oasis","mutanus","naralex","verdan"},rel={"npc:naralex","topic:druids-of-the-fang","npc:mutanus-the-devourer","quest:914","subzone:lushwater-oasis","topic:emerald-dream","npc:lord-serpentis","zone:barrens"},m={levels="17-24"},src={"Wailing Caverns"}}
